KG42.register("source_edge_archive-133d6849df42cac303b203d7",{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E005","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E005","source":"settlement.payment","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C005"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-dddaa2edb4acd670","target":"COMP-20e312b579d3a493","source_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","target_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","target_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"74eff9b7a918a1e6676e7ac0b7e32aeb91f89c41c8a19883499b3e175ee7785e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Monetary obligations, transfers, sharing or settlement conditions in this mechanism: ESP computes internal buying/selling prices from supply-demand ratio and grid tariffs; prosumers iteratively reschedule; preserve service-fee and balance conditions.","target_definition":"Internal prices are tariff-bounded functions of the zone supply-demand ratio, with distinct buying/selling roles for net power signs. For SDR above one both equal the export tariff; for SDR between zero and one retain the source nonlinear selling-price formula and buying-price cost/balance construction. Do not generalize denominator limits or fee accounting beyond source conditions.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The internal buying-price construction takes account of internal energy-sale costs, utility-grid charges and ESP charges. Scope: Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g03-E18"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"der When SDR = 0, which means no PV prosumer sells power, ded the required energy is bought from the","equation_id":"(10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Secondly, the internal buying price is defined as an average value considering the cost of internal selling energy, utility grid's charge and the ESP's charge: Pr_{buy}^{h} = f(SDR^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h} \\cdot SDR^{h} + \\lambda_{buy}(1 - SDR^{h}), & 0 \\leq SDR^{h} \\leq 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell}, & SDR > 1 \\end{cases}   (10)  When 0 \u003c SDR^{h} \u003c 1, the total power demand exceeds the total power supply of PV systems in the energy sharing zone, the lacking power is bought from the utility grid at the price of \\lambda_{buy}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E005","source":"settlement.payment","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"paper_scope_note":"Retain the positive and negative net-power branches, ESP organizational responsibilities, cost valuation, and the shared service fee sub-item; the iterative price, final price, and grid trading after failure cannot be treated as identical."}});
